# IT 140 Module Three Assignment
# Paycheck Calculator Pseudocode Template
#
# Replace every TODO prompt with your own pseudocode.
# Keep this file in .pseudo format for submission.
#
# Your finished pseudocode should represent the same logic as your flowchart.
# Use clear indentation and ALLCAPS pseudocode keywords, such as GET (input),
# PUT (output), LET (assignment), IF, ELSE, and ENDIF where they fit your design.

START paycheck_calculator

   GET "employee" name from user.
   GET "hours" from user, LET "hours" to allow for decimals. 
   GET "rate" from rubric, LET "rate" to be hardcoded
   GET "Overtime_rate", LET "overtime_rate" with half of "rate" multipied by "rate" 
    

    IF "hours" is greater than zero and less than or equal to forty.
        LET "pay" with "hours" multiplied by "rate"
        PUT "employee"('s) paycheck: ($)"pay"

    ELIF "hours" is greater than forty 
        LET "overtime_hours" equal "hours" minus forty
        LET "pay" equal "rate" multiplied by forty, plus "overtime_hours" multiplied by "rate"
        PUT "employee"('s) paycheck: ($)"pay"
    else
        PUT ""Invalid entries""


END paycheck_calculator



